  "//@ai-sdk/anthropic": "PINNED EXACTLY on purpose. Three hand-copied mirrors (packages/types assistant-provider-settings, assistant-contract runtime-data, agent types) name the installed version, and nothing checks them against it. An exact pin confines a change to a deliberate bump PR. REVIEW TRIGGER: raise it in a deliberate bump, re-read the provider's thinking and effort shapes, and correct the three mirrors in the same change. Cost, stated: this forfeits automatic patch and security uptake for this package.",
  "//@ai-sdk/openai": "Exact pin: 4.0.96 uses the declared openai.tool_search provider identity for hosted history (vercel/ai#19754, shipped in 4.0.50). The old regression fixture omitted that declaration; keep it explicit and preserve all distinct call/output ID assertions and ordinary-function controls when bumping. Keep the Mastra hydration compatibility fix. Production discovery remains Brainstrike-owned. Resolve this workspace copy, not Bedrock's nested OpenAI client; preserve the undici security floor.",
